  dialogue: [
    { speaker: 'Rector',    text: 'Good morning. I\'ve called this briefing to address the questions that have been circulating about the new English language requirement.',       isLeft: false },
    { speaker: 'Reporter 1',text: 'Rector, can you confirm whether all students will be required to pass a B2 English assessment to graduate?',                                   isLeft: true  },
    { speaker: 'Rector',    text: 'The university has decided that from the 2027 intake, students will need to demonstrate B2 English proficiency. However, this applies to new students only. Current students are not affected.',  isLeft: false },
    { speaker: 'Reporter 2',text: 'Some faculty members have suggested this would put additional pressure on students from non-urban areas. How do you respond?',                  isLeft: true  },
    { speaker: 'Rector',    text: 'We acknowledge that access to English-language preparation varies across regions. That\'s why we\'re announcing today that the university will fund English preparation courses for all first-year students from next autumn.',  isLeft: false },
    { speaker: 'Reporter 1',text: 'Did you consult students before making this decision?',                                                                                         isLeft: true  },
    { speaker: 'Rector',    text: 'The student council was informed of the proposal in February and was invited to provide feedback. Their feedback was considered during the final decision-making process.',  isLeft: false },
    { speaker: 'Reporter 2',text: 'The student council president has claimed that they were not given sufficient time to respond properly. Do you dispute that?',                  isLeft: true  },
    { speaker: 'Rector',    text: 'I wouldn\'t say "dispute." I\'d say that the timeline was challenging, and I accept that the consultation process could have been longer. We intend to improve this for future policy decisions.',  isLeft: false },
    { speaker: 'Reporter 1',text: 'Will students who fail the B2 assessment be denied graduation?',                                                                                isLeft: true  },
    { speaker: 'Rector',    text: 'Students who do not meet the requirement will be offered additional support and multiple assessment opportunities. We have no intention of withholding graduation from students who make genuine effort.',  isLeft: false },
    { speaker: 'Reporter 2',text: 'Finally, what would you say to students who are worried about this change?',                                                                    isLeft: true  },
    { speaker: 'Rector',    text: 'I\'d tell them that this requirement reflects the reality of the professional world they are entering. English proficiency is not an add-on — it is a core professional skill. And I would assure them that the university will support them in achieving it.',  isLeft: false },
  ],

