  grammarTip: "Advanced Passive Structures:\n\nREPORTING VERBS — 2 structures:\nA: It IS SAID THAT he is the best.\nB: He IS SAID TO BE the best.\n\nWith past reference:\n\"She IS BELIEVED TO HAVE DISCOVERED the error.\"\n(present belief about past action → perfect infinitive)\n\nIMPERSONAL PASSIVE for scientific consensus:\n\"It HAS BEEN ESTABLISHED that...\"\n\"It IS WIDELY ACCEPTED that...\"\n\"It HAS BEEN DEMONSTRATED that...\"\n\nBE SUPPOSED TO = expectation:\n\"You ARE SUPPOSED TO submit by Friday.\"\n\"The meeting WAS SUPPOSED TO start at 3.\"\n(expectation, often not met)\n\nCAUSATIVE (have/get something done):\nhave + obj + pp\n\"She HAD her essay PROOFREAD.\"\n\"I need to GET my laptop REPAIRED.\"\n→ Someone else does it for you",

