  grammarTip: "Present Perfect Continuous:\nhave/has + been + V-ing\n\nUSE PPC for:\n→ DURATION (how long something has been happening)\n  \"I\'ve been waiting FOR two hours.\"\n  \"She\'s been studying SINCE this morning.\"\n\n→ ONGOING PROCESS (still in progress)\n  \"He\'s been writing all day — not finished yet.\"\n\n→ EXPLAINING VISIBLE STATE\n  \"You look tired — have you been running?\"\n\nCHOOSE PPS INSTEAD when:\n→ Counting: \"She\'s WRITTEN 3 papers.\" ✅\n→ Result matters: \"I\'ve FINISHED.\" ✅\n→ Stative verb: \"I\'ve KNOWN her.\" ✅\n\nBOTH possible (different emphasis):\n\"I\'ve worked here for 3 years.\" (achievement)\n\"I\'ve been working here for 3 years.\" (ongoing)\n\nKey question: RESULT or PROCESS?\n→ Result focus = PPS\n→ Process focus = PPC",

